======================================================================
POINT 2. "Payment sent" pressed twice at the same moment
======================================================================
Problem: markPaymentSent checked the order, then wrote SUBMITTED by id alone. Two clicks at
         the same moment both passed the checks: two "payment sent" chat messages and two
         emails to the admin. The admin's "Ask for a new proof" had the same gap (two
         "please send a new proof" messages to the customer).
Fix:     new repository function OrderRepository.changePaymentStatus(id, from, to): a
         compare-and-swap that only changes a PENDING order whose payment is still one of
         `from` (same pattern as the stock and status code). The second click matches
         nothing: the customer sees "You already told us you've paid"; the admin sees
         "There's no payment waiting to be checked." Nothing else is written or sent.
Files:   src/prisma/orders.ts, src/services/orders.ts
Tests:   "[fixed] two 'Payment sent' clicks at the same moment tell the store only once"
         "asks for a new proof only when one is waiting, and only once"

======================================================================
POINT 3. Switched-off products readable through the cart
======================================================================
Problem: getCartLinesAction (public) returned the name and price of a product the admin had
         switched off, to anyone who knew its id. The product page itself already hid it.
Fix:     CatalogService.getCartLines skips inactive products, exactly like deleted ones. A
         customer who still has one in their cart sees the existing "product removed" line
         (no name, no price) and can't check out until they remove it, as before.
Files:   src/services/catalog.ts
Tests:   "[fixed] says nothing about a product the admin switched off, even with its id"
         (new file src/services/catalog.test.ts, also: 50-line cap, removed option)

======================================================================
POINT 4. STAFF role: orders + chat only
======================================================================
Rule (src/lib/roles.ts: TEAM = ADMIN + STAFF, isTeam()):
  STAFF can:      open /admin/orders and each order, chat with customers (messages are signed
                  with the staff member's name for the team), see payment proofs, confirm or
                  change an order's status, ask for a new proof, send delivery emails, manage
                  shipments (list, new, edit, timeline), and use "Manage" on /order/<id>.
  ADMIN only:     dashboard (sales figures, availability switch), products, categories,
                  reviews, refunds ("Mark refunded" button hidden for staff, action refused).
  How it looks:   staff see only "Orders" and "Shipments" in the admin menu; /admin sends them
                  to /admin/orders; the "Admin" link in the store header shows for staff too.
  Not changed:    new-order and payment emails still go to ADMIN accounts only (or to
                  ADMIN_NOTIFY_EMAIL). Nobody can make themselves STAFF: the role is not
                  accepted from sign-up or profile forms (auth config unchanged).
Files:   src/lib/roles.ts, src/app/admin/layout.tsx, src/app/admin/page.tsx,
         src/app/admin/orders/page.tsx, src/app/admin/orders/[id]/page.tsx,
         src/app/admin/shipments/{page,[id]/page,new/page}.tsx, src/components/admin/AdminNav.tsx,
         src/actions/orders.ts, src/actions/messages.ts, src/actions/shipments.ts,
         src/services/messages.ts, src/services/orders.ts, src/app/(store)/order/[id]/page.tsx,
         src/components/layout/Header.tsx, CLAUDE.md
Tests:   src/actions/access.test.ts: 15 admin-only actions refuse guest/customer/staff;
         9 team actions refuse guest/customer and work for staff and admin.
         src/test/access-rules.test.ts: the exact list of pages staff may open (a new page
         for staff must be added there on purpose).
         src/services/messages.test.ts, orders.test.ts: staff can use the chat, see photos
         and see orders.

